 "notes": "Fig. 3: 95% C.L. exclusion on (ma, g_agamma) from photon-ALP oscillation fits to Tibet ASgamma + HAWC + MAGIC + HEGRA Crab Nebula gamma-ray spectra (total chi2 < 53.4 criterion). Curve is the lower boundary (lower envelope) of the main filled exclusion contour extracted from the vector paths of the e-print figure crab_result_axion.pdf; axis calibration cross-checked against the CAST line drawn at 6.6e-11 GeV^-1. Matches quoted result g_agamma < 1.8e-10 GeV^-1 for ma = 2e-7 to 6e-7 eV. A smaller disconnected excluded island at ma ~ 2.7e-8 to 9.6e-8 eV, g ~ 1.7e-10 to 5.9e-10 GeV^-1 is not included in data_points. Limit is from photon propagation in the Galactic B-field and does not depend on the local DM density (the paper's separate dark-photon epsilon limit, which assumed rho_DM = 0.3 GeV/cm^3, is not the reported curve).",
